/-!
# The first outer M₁₂ parabolic and its nonsplit two-core

For `m : InnerModel`, the centralizer H of the original `z` has order 384,
its intrinsic two-core has order 64, and H/O₂(H) is actually isomorphic to
S₃ and PSL₂(2). The ambient image of [O₂(H),O²(H)] is exactly the subgroup
generated by the original two quaternion pairs, an extraspecial group of
order 32. The certified factor-swap lift has square `z`; adjoining it to
that quaternion subgroup gives the actual nonsplit two-core.

The original Z = ⟨z⟩ is the center of this core. The intrinsic quotient
O₂(H)/Z is identified with E₄ wr C₂, taking the quaternion-core image to the
wreath base. Its H-action is actual conjugation, with all normalization
premises discharged and both original quaternion markings retained. The
original natural four is transported through the same marked embedding.

The core has twenty square-one elements, all in the quaternion subgroup;
the existing split model has twenty-eight. Neither the cores nor the whole
parabolics are isomorphic. The center has order two, so the printed central
product C₄ * Q₈² is impossible for this subgroup. These distinctions are
proved without relying on GAP group labels. The only remaining external
input of this conditional interface is the explicitly stipulated InnerModel;
the full automorphism identification and source amalgam assembly belong to
their respective consumers.

Sources: Aschbacher--Smith, E.2.16, F.1.12(I)(13), and 14.2.21,
`refs/quasithin.pdf`, printed pp.228, 263, 988.
-/
